WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.930
STRIKE THE STRATEGIC SATELLITE

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.130
"Strike the Strategic Satellite".

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:26.760
STRIKE THE STRATEGIC SATELLITE

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.660
Look at all the fire lines and fireballs!

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.000
The battle's in full swing now?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.730
Correct course right, one degree.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:50.800
Roger!

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.330
Why'd Elisha stay behind on the Aeneas?

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.400
Why can't you understand that she's not cut out for battle?

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.400
So, Martina likes battle, then?

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.500
It's hard keeping the lenses steady! Be quiet!

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.700
Yeah, quit talking!

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:08.330
All right!

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.600
I just wanted to be by Elisha's side.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:17.500
Huh? Odelo, aren't you dedicating your life to the League Militaire's battle?

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.600
Damn, was my radio on?

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.960
We're already in combat.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.860
Of course you have normal suit radios on open channel.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.160
Right, so we can talk to each other at all times.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.530
W-We're getting close...

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.730
The advance Javelin team's in a tough fight with Keilas Guilie.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.760
Losing ground.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:50.260
Have Strike Team and the Gundams cover the Gaunland's forward airspace.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:55.030
This will all be pointless if it gets sunk before reaching Keilas Guilie.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.330
Did I get caught in the nuke blasts?!

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.230
Dammit, Üso! He's still not used to team combat.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.400
Junko Jenko, take care of Üso!

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.230
Roger!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.260
Don't be in a hurry to die, Junko.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.260
You need a new gimmick!

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.900
Miss Junko?

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.330
We're in the melee combat zone! Are you taking a nap, kid?!

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.830
How about you quit fighting like you want to die, Miss Junko?!

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.900
Don't speak to me that way!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.100
What's wrong? Where's your usual spirit?

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:11.460
I'm the same as always.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.260
It's possible that that Shahkti girl was rescued by one of the enemy ships.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.060
I've thought of that, too!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.760
Then we need to capture their ships!

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:26.500
Capture a whole enemy ship? There's no way we could.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.260
Out of the way!

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.730
That's the spirit!

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.000
Miss Junko...

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.830
The beam pistol doesn't have much power unless I get close! Right!

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.560
You want to attack? Then get over here!

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.460
Getting serious is never easy.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.200
Those are Junko and Üso's units.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.460
Marbet, you play rear guard.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.630
Roger!

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:24.030
Once again, Üso's in front and I'm in the rear.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:29.760
Marbet!

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.400
Marbet, why are you hesitating?

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.660
I'm not!

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:43.830
Good!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.360
Have I become some kind of awful woman?

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.830
I can't hit it!

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.330
If I don't hit it, I'm dead! I'll never see Shahkti again!

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.100
Hit it!

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:11.900
What?!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.560
I heard something.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.230
But what?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.130
It was like the screech of a life being crushed.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.760
Üso doesn't have a beam rifle!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.760
Odelo, get a weapon to the Gundam!

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.000
I'll pass it to him.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.300
I'll help, too!

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:41.630
Trying to show off for Martina, huh, Warren?

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:46.830
Well, you're not too enthusiastic, since Elisha isn't here, Odelo.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.360
I'm helping because I'm moved by...

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.800
...the League Militaire's battle, not because of some girl!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.960
I didn't realize!

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:56.130
Those two...

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.530
It's all about Elisha and Martina, huh?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.400
They don't get why we're fighting the Zanscare, do they?

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:06.060
Being a man means you get the job done,

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.560
even when you know you'll die doing it.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.760
I know, which is why I'm out here!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.760
Good attitude.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:26.500
Tomáš, the spare weapons are detached. Signal Üso!

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:27.830
Roger!

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:34.960
It's no use.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.130
I'm afraid of the sound of life being crushed!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.400
What's that light?

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.300
That light has the warmth of my friends.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.660
Odelo? Tomáš and the others?!

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.300
Trying to kill me?!

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.700
Tomáš and the others brought me weapons.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.130
They got your overhang cannons?

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.330
They didn't get the main unit, though.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.560
Looks that way. Take what you want.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.760
They're just old weapons, though.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.060
But their batteries have been properly changed, so they're usable.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.100
Thanks.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.500
I think that clothesline pole thing will fit the Victory's hand.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.160
It should come in handy. Thanks.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.900
Warren, I need some reinforcement putty!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.530
Right!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.760
Where it's burned.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.360
Gotcha. How's that?

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.300
Exactly!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.600
The rest are okay!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.700
A clothesline pole, huh?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.930
Odelo, Warren, Martina, I'm leaving. You ready?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.430
Is he ready to go?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.760
Üso, your number 1 tail nozzle cover's a little loose.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.830
It shouldn't be as problem if I keep the swing within 10 degrees.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.200
Good job, Warren.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:03.100
Right.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.530
All set, Üso!

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.200
Odelo, calm down!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.300
Darn it, Odelo! You and Martina?!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.530
You made contact with the Fishbone?

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.560
Yeah, they're great backup support.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.530
Yes, they are.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.730
How are things going for you and the others, Miss Junko?

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:25.660
What do you mean?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.160
You and Mr. Oliver and Marbet.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.360
Nothing for a kid to worry about. Here they come!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.600
Everyone went through a lot of trouble to get me these weapons.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.230
Time to test them!

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.100
Take this!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.960
Don't play with your weapons! Killing people isn't a game!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.860
I'm making a game out of killing people?

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:15.060
No. I'd never do that!

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.600
It's because the enemy came! They're the enemy, right?!

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:22.900
Maybe, but I'm trying to tell you how to confront them like a pilot.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:27.800
If you're too flashy, you give away your position.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:31.900
Right. Think like a pilot. Position...

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:36.200
A Newtype isn't controlled by transient emotions, right?

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.400
Right!

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.830
Use the clothesline pole when we reach Keilas Guilie.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.060
Right!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:50.000
And don't you go throwing your life away, Miss Junko.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.660
Their firepower hasn't lessened a bit!

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.030
What was that fireball?

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.960
It might be Üso destroying more enemy units.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.800
Huh? That kid?

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.860
That boy is a combat genius.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.630
I've stuck with you this far...

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.330
...because I'm curious about what sort of kid he is.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:26.400
Huh? Huh?

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.930
We've closed ranged with the Keilas Guilie Fleet, haven't we?

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.800
How's the Gaunland's remote control?

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.800
Lieutenant Gomez!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:33.730
Yeah?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.430
If we've closed range, shouldn't we use the remote to charge them?

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.960
The Gaunland is unmanned, after all.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.100
Mr. Otis, hurry!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.260
I'm doing it.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.230
Coordination of the mobile suit units at the front line is lax!

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:52.100
Yes, sir!

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.030
Hasn't Squid 2 left for the homeland yet?

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.500
It's holding its ground.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.230
Dammit, Cronicle!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.900
Lt. Cronicle, you're going out?

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.630
Don't worry.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.900
How do Units 2 and 3 look?

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.260
No go, although we were able to start the engines.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.800
Open the forward hatch. I'll go out alone.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.330
Contio 1 is moving out!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.460
That broken-down ship has come to die.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.260
Cronicle, Contio 1, moving out!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.200
The Gaunland's remote control is working.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:46.600
It's time.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.500
Okay, cut the Gaunland's barrier!

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.860
Where are our defense mobile suits?!

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.800
Are they just going to allow the League Militaire to advance?!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.000
Isn't it glorious?!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:23.560
If we charge as I've ordered, it'll work! It'll work!

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.200
Give me a break...

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:27.530
Otis, back off the attack a bit.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:29.400
Gomez, I'm giving the orders here!

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.530
Intensify barrage! Intensify!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.660
Facing the Keilas Guilie Fleet with only two ships?!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.400
What the... That beam just now wasn't like the others!

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.230
The enemy ships have entered our airspace?!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.060
Concentrate our forces in front of the Squid!

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:05.930
Captain Tassilo, please, it's time you put on a normal suit!

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.060
I've no intention of losing here!

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.830
Just as we planned!

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.960
The enemy's concentrating their forces on the Gaunland!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.760
Prepare for ship to ship combat!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.500
Get ready to self-destruct the Gaunland.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.730
Self-destruct?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.560
Leave the timing to me.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.660
A direct hit?! No, not just that!

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.860
One ship, down! Now for another...

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.330
Two ships, destroyed!

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.430
Don't panic! This is war!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.830
The Reineforce is closing in from the rear!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.260
Closing in? What are they doing?

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.660
Our mobile suit units are too scattered!

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.630
Come in! Regroup!

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.830
It's closing in, huh.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:09.900
Closing in!

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.700
Prepare for ship-to-ship combat.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.300
Ship-to-ship?

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.460
Something's coming!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:20.100
The Gaunland in front was a dummy?!

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:21.430
What? A dummy?

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:23.030
Keep your eyes on that enemy ship!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:23.660
Sir!

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.930
They decoyed us! Intercept!

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.030
It's too close! Our support mobile suits can't stop it-

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:34.460
Arm yourselves with machine guns and small arms.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.900
Fight them as circumstances demand!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.830
We're being boarded.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.200
Boarded?!

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.330
Boarded.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.800
Don't falter! Onward!

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:51.930
All hands, prepare to board them!

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.900
One old wreck controlling another via remote control, huh?

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.830
Confine targets to the Reineforce!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:08.100
Reineforce is about to contact the enemy vessel!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.730
Now that they've made contact, we'll have to evacuate!

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.600
Neither our mobile suits nor theirs can do anything, now!

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:23.530
Prepare to repel boarders! Hand-to-hand!

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.430
Sir!

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.600
The princess is aboard that ship.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.160
We cannot afford any avoidable losses.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:34.500
We'll secure an escape path while we fight them hand-to-hand.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.230
Evacuate our troops in the rear line vessels.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.430
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:44.530
Did my plan to conquer Earth depend too much on Keilas Guilie?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.960
Our firing line's too weak! Why aren't we attacking the Squid?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.730
What's this?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.230
Take it. We're about to fight hand-to-hand.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.730
In mobile suits?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.800
Actual hand-to-hand between actual soldiers.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.630
No... Real hand-to-hand combat?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.200
I don't want this!

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.000
All hands, retreat!

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:08.460
Open an escape route!

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.300
Take the bridge!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.760
C'mon, hurry up!

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:20.860
What are you doing?! Retreat to the next ship!

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.400
Surrender!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.730
The engine looks dangerously close to overheating!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.300
A nuclear explosion?!

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.460
If it's built according to international standards,

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.900
you can just cut the control lines!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.400
Everyone, move in to the enemy ship!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:35.700
Haro! Haro!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.200
Captain Tassilo!

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.060
Where's Captain Tassilo?

00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:00.100
Good work, Captain Gomez. So, he's boarded the enemy ship?

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:03.760
Once the soldiers move in, there's nothing we can do.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.000
They've latched on to Keilas Guilie!

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:10.300
Where's Üso?!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:11.330
The enemy!

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:14.530
Captain Tassilo!

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.630
Are our soldiers moving?

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.630
They're evacuating as they fight!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:18.460
Good!

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:19.700
Captain Tassilo!

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.800
Cronicle?

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.130
You're all right, sir! Please, get into my suit's hand.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.530
Okay, do it!

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.860
Looks like they don't want to let us go.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.330
That pink one isn't getting away!

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:49.900
I'm not dead yet!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.030
Again and again! It's pissing me off!

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.060
Marbet, what are you doing?!

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.530
Junko, stop being so reckless!

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.130
Protecting our flesh and blood soldiers comes first!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.030
A fleeing enemy is a wounded beast! They can be frightening!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.960
That's true, but all the more reason to kill them!

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.630
I can't just let you get yourself killed now!

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.730
You and Miss Marbet...

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:18.760
I understand, Marbet.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.030
Haro!

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:29.330
Can you hear me, Pilot?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:30.160
What?

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:33.300
Do you know a pilot named Üso Ewin?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:34.430
Who is this?

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.800
If you do, tell him that Shahkti and the others are okay.

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.430
Who are you?

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:40.360
I'm...

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.600
Doing this in the storage room is hopeless!

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.160
That's not true.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.160
What if they find us?

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.730
Just as long as somebody notices this!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:13.630
Haro!

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.660
Flashing!

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:22.130
Found her! Found Shahkti!

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.130
Haro!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.360
Haro!

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.760
Haro, tell Üso that we're all right!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:32.330
Tell everyone, Haro!

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:33.160
Haro!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.160
What about that enemy ship?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.130
It's taking their soldiers aboard and retreating.

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:44.930
How's the anti-air weaponry?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:47.700
Ness and Striker and the others are handling them.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:08.030
Hey, we won, didn't we?

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:09.130
Yeah!

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:11.760
I'm so happy!

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.330
I can't believe how happy I am!

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:15.360
I'm also really happy, right now!

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.100
Marbet?

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:19.960
Yeah?

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.900
Thanks to you, I can drink my favorite lemonade some more.

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:25.230
May I join you?

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.100
Of course.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.060
Thanks.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:31.330
Adults are good at compromising.

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:33.300
Is that what makes them adults?

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.430
What?

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:35.860
It's good, right?

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:37.200
I guess.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.800
Üso, I got a strange message.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:40.560
Huh?

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.760
That Shahkti and the others are all right.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.160
Shahkti and the others are okay?!

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:48.100
A woman's voice contacted me during the battle and asked me to tell you, Üso.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:52.830
A woman's voice? Whose?

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:55.800
She was wearing a BESPA normal suit, so I don't know.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:00.400
It was Miss Katejina! Miss Katejina told her!

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:01.960
Yeah!

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.600
Shahkti's alive!

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:08.300
She's alive!

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:12.100
Yeah!!!

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:38.330
Üso is reunited with Mr. Godwald, the BESPA pilot he met before.

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:44.500
But it comes amidst a battle on which both stake their lives...

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:49.500
A battle between soldiers fighting to survive, and pass on what's in their hearts.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:53.400
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:56.500
"The Tiger of Space".

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:57.860
Please watch it!
